<title>JAPAN: Toyota Oct domestic output up 20.2% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Toyota Oct domestic output up 20.2% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Toyota Motor Corp said on Wednesday that its domestic vehicle production, exports, domestic sales, and overseas output in October were as follows:</p>
<p> Production	  337,181   up  20.2 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		285,947   up  25.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     51,234   down 3.0 percent</p>
<p> Domestic sales    197,671   up   8.3 percent</p>
<p>  - Car		136,815   up   8.6 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     60,856   up   7.8 percent</p>
<p> Exports	     124,145   up  27.2 percent</p>
<p>  - Cars		96,634   up  35.9 percent</p>
<p>  - Truck &amp; Bus     27,511   up   3.8 percent</p>
<p> Overseas output   138,809   up  19.2 percent</p>
<p>It was the fourth successive month that domestic production gained on a year-on-year basis, reflecting strong domestic sales of its new models. It was the sixth successive month that exports gained on a year-on-year basis, helped by a weaker yen.</p>
<p>It was the second successive month that domestic sales rose on a year-on-year basis, while it was the also the second successive month that overseas production rose on a year-on-year basis.</p>
</text>
